<title>INDIA: India considers tax breaks for telecom companies.</title>
<headline>India considers tax breaks for telecom companies.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian government is contemplating the grant of an &quot;infrastructure status&quot; to the telecommunication sector with the aim of giving it tax concessions, the Press Trust of India (PTI) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A proposal for this is being finalised and would be presented to the Finance Ministry for approval, the news agency quoted A.V.Gokak, chairman of the government's Telecom Commission, as saying.</p>
